    {
      "fingerprint": "e90f641d7bbade70aa4bce5d919ce6ee5f1d652a69aa020125a02d075c1b0068",
      "note": "params[:wizard_id] reaches a file path, and the route segment does not stop traversal. wizards/:wizard_id excludes a literal / and ., but the segment is percent-decoded after routing, so GET /wizards/%2e%2e%2fwizard%2fresearchwrite.json returns 200 and serves the traversed file. (An earlier version of this note claimed such payloads are rejected at routing with a 404; that is true only for unencoded ones, and was corrected during review of #7085.) Baselined because the filename is pinned to wizard.yml, so the reachable set is files named exactly wizard.yml -- on a deployed host, only this repo's five config/wizard/*/wizard.yml, which this unauthenticated endpoint already serves in full. Content is parsed with YAML.safe_load and rendered as JSON. A traversal to a directory with no wizard.yml returns 500 rather than disclosing anything. Revisit if the filename ever becomes dynamic, if the id arrives from a query parameter or a globbed route, or if anything not already public is ever named wizard.yml."
    },
    {
      "fingerprint": "aa5a2b411ef7e82ff5efb110835fd92044784037fd878563b5b14ea4f859d1ad",
      "note": "LEADING_COLON_MATCHER and SPECIAL_PAGE_MATCHER are deliberately first-character checks, so the \\z anchor Brakeman recommends does not apply to them."
    },
    {
      "fingerprint": "b73ad3b228b6ae84a1a27f15d57b0f9a550cd70dc17df6bfb49e246f4256bbff",
      "note": "The confusion resolves in the safe direction: a HEAD request is treated as non-GET, so respond_to_non_get_request returns the stub 200 instead of running the enrollment path."
    },
    {
      "fingerprint": "ae4a8d5fd6d2f7d021db881f34b1cb74df0f222c816d2442614ea36e48827c6e",
      "note": "Here :role is the assignment role (0 assigned / 1 reviewing), not a privilege level, and the controller requires course participation."
    },
    {
      "fingerprint": "6f4564c6038e6ebc8438fb0029c85bef24e53deafb128ee2dfa000dcebc827ea",
      "note": "Permitting :role is intentional, and authority over it is now enforced: ensure_management_role_is_authorized requires the requester to be an instructor in the course, or an admin, before either role in User::EDITING_ROLES (instructor, Wiki Ed staff) can be granted or removed. Those are the roles that make can_edit? true. Covered by spec/controllers/users/enrollment_role_authorization_spec.rb."
    },
